  - [1mA JS render function[0m — a small [38;5;153mcreateCheckbox(label)[39m (or equivalent) that builds the element, plus an array of items
    to render. Costs a [38;5;153m<script>[39m block and an item model, but adding items is data, not markup. This is the one that's
    expensive to retrofit later if you start static and grow.

  Persistence across reload is a separate question I'll ask after this one; it's cheap to add either way.

  [1mMy recommendation: static markup only.[0m You said basic and nothing fancy, and a native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m already
  gives you on/off state with no code. Going to JS is easy later; the reverse is the throwaway.

